course: dictionary
lesson: 2502
title: Debt: money you owe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A debt is money that you owe to someone. You borrowed it, so you must give it back. «To borrow is to take money you must give back; debt is the money you still owe.» Debt is a noun: a debt, debts.
explain: Debt can be shown with numbers. If you have £5 but owe £8, you are £3 in debt. We write this as a negative number, because once the debt is counted you have less than nothing.
explain: «Paying back £10 a week clears a £50 debt in £50 ÷ £10 = 5 weeks.» Each week you pay £10, so the debt gets smaller until it is gone. To repay means to pay it back, and to pay off a debt means to finish paying it.
explain: Debt can also mean a feeling. A debt of gratitude means you owe someone thanks for their help. Context tells you which meaning is meant: money you owe, the state of owing money, or a thank-you feeling.
fact: A debt is money that you owe to someone.
fact: To be in debt means you currently owe money. To be out of debt means you owe nothing.
fact: Borrowing on a credit card or a loan creates debt, which must be paid back, usually with interest.
fact: «Some debt can help, like a mortgage for a home; debt for things you can't afford, like an unpaid credit card, can trap people.»
fact: To get into debt means to start owing money. To pay off a debt means to pay all of it back.
exercise: You have £5 and you owe £8. What does it mean to be £3 in debt? | You saved £3 in a jar | You spent £3 on sweets today | You have £3 more than nothing | *You owe £3 more than you have
exercise: «Paying back £10 a week clears a £50 debt in £50 ÷ £10 = 5 weeks.» How many weeks does it take? | 50 weeks | *5 weeks | 2 weeks | 10 weeks
exercise: Zara says, «I'm in debt to my brother for lending me £4.» What does debt mean here? | A present he gave her | A thank-you card | *Money she must pay back to her brother | A game she owes him
test: What does «to repay» mean? | To borrow money | To save money in a box | To spend money quickly | *To pay money back
test: Which sentence shows a debt of gratitude? | Your bike has a flat tyre | *You feel you owe a friend thanks for helping you | You have a £5 note in your wallet | You owe a shop £10 for a toy
exam: Which statement matches «Some debt can help, like a mortgage for a home»? | A mortgage is a free gift from the bank | *Some debt can be useful, such as borrowing to buy a home | Debt only matters to people who shop | All debt is always bad and must be avoided
